      "description": "Career Services 1.888.790.8080 admissions@amridgeuniversity.edu Admissions Apply for Admission Military First Responders Corporate Alliance Early Credit and Dual Enrollment Request your Official Transcript Academics Programs of Study College of Business and Leadership AA in Business Administration AA in Human Resource Leadership AA Information Systems Management AA Web Development BS Business Administration BS Human Resource Leadership BS Information Systems Management BS Management MA in Interdisciplinary Studies Master of Business Administration (MBA) MS Leadership and Management PhD in Interdisciplinary Studies PhD Organizational Leadership and Management College of General Studies AA in Criminal Justice AA in Human Development AA in Legal Studies AA in Liberal Studies BS in Criminal Justice BS in Human Development Minor in Family and Consumer Sciences School of Education and Human Services MA in Interdisciplinary Studies MA in Marriage and Family Therapy MA in Professional Counseling MDiv in Marriage and Family Therapy MDiv in Professional Counseling MS Human Services Doctor of Ministry in Family Therapy I Doctor of Ministry in Family Therapy II EdD in Higher Education Administration PhD in Interdisciplinary Studies PhD in Professional Counseling PhD in Marriage and Family Therapy Turner School of Theology AA in Ministry/Bible BA in Biblical Studies BS in Ministry/Bible Professional Studies Graduate Certificate in Ministry MA in Interdisciplinary Studies MA in Christian Education MA in New Testament Studies MA in Old Testament Studies MS in Christian Ministry MS Ministerial Leadership Master of Divinity Master of Divinity Ministerial Leadership Doctor of Ministry PhD in Interdisciplinary Studies Doctor of Philosophy in Biblical Studies Professional Licensure Academic Catalog 2026-2027 Academic Calendar 2026-2027 Course Schedules Continuing Education Library Financial Aid Student Financial Aid Center Tuition & Fees Scholarships Student Services Registrar Graduation Career Services Books Amridge Spirit Shop Amridge Laptop Program Title IX About Amridge Contact Us Giving and Advancement Amridge University Press MyAmridge Register for Classes Self Service Amridge Announcements Canvas Login IT Help Desk Get Started Today! Career Services Home Student Services Career Services Welcome to the Career Service Center Amridge University Career Services Center offers various career-related services and resources to assist students and alums in developing and implementing their career plans. The university’s Career Services Portal offers Career Advice, access to current Job Postings, and Internships. Additionally, students and alumni are given access to Resume Writing Services with support from the Career Services staff, Online workshops, and Career Fairs. Career Assistance: Allow a Career Advisor to guide you through the tools that are nenter that career you desire on the right foot. Career Search: Search for job postings that companies have posted and search a national database using NACElink. Employer Database: A directory of employers registered with Amridge University looking for students and alums to fill positions at their company. Resource Library: Informational documents to help before, during, and after an interview. This also includes sample resumes and cover letters. Resume Builder: This tool helps you build your resume based on your career field, guides you through the sections that should be completed on a resume, and even allows you to choose a format. Resume Review: After creating your resume, cover letter, or thank you letter, submit it for our Career Services Representative to review. Informational Videos: Learn how to land an interview, how to get ready for an interview, and what to bring with you to an interview. Login to Career Services Student Career Services Login Employer Career Services Login Enhance Your Job Prospects with \"Promote Me\" Are you ready to stand out to top employers? With Symplicity’s “Promote Me” service, you can increase your visibility and connect with companies actively searching for candidates like you! By opting into this feature, your resume and profile will be accessible to recruiters and hiring managers looking for students with your skills and qualifications. This is an easy and effective way to get noticed without applying for every job individually! 🚀 Why use “Promote Me”? ✔ Get discovered by top employers ✔ Open doors to exclusive job opportunities ✔ Save time while expanding your career prospects Don’t miss out on this opportunity to jump-start your career! If you have questions or have not logged into the Amridge Career Services portal to begin using these services, contact careerservices@amridgeuniversity.edu for assistance. Student Public Profile Create a professional presence online in your Career Services portal! Track experiences early in your college career or use the Resume Builder to populate the profile when you are ready to start your job search. The Public Profile helps students track their LER (learning and employment records) and break down skills. Acts to connect students to the larger Symplicity Recruit Network. > Learn More about the Steps to Create your Profile Learning Styles An assessment of your learning style will help you understand information and solve problems while you learn. Take the FREE learning styles test! How can we help you? Meet Our Staff Dr. Patsy Moretz, Career Services Coordinator If you have questions or have not logged into the Amridge Career Services portal to begin using these services, contact careerservices@amridgeuniversity.edu for assistance. SACSCOC Accreditation Amridge University, Inc. is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC) to award associate, baccalaureate, masters, and doctorate degrees. Amridge University also may offer credentials such as certificates and diplomas at approved degree levels. Questions about the accreditation of Amridge University, Inc. may be directed in writing to the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges at 1866 Southern Lane, Decatur, GA  30033-4097, by calling (404) 679-4500, or by using information available on SACSCOC’s website (www.sacscoc.org). Mission and Purpose Amridge University is an independent, coeducational institution dedicated to the spirit of its Christian ideals and heritage. With a commitment to academic excellence, distance education, and spiritual vitality, Amridge University’s mission is to prepare men and women for a lifetime of learning, leadership, and service to their professions, society, church, and family, through teaching, learning experiences and support services. Institutional Purpose In keeping with its Christian heritage, Amridge University provides educational opportunities through five schools: (1) College of Business and Leadership, (2) College of General Studies, (3) School of Human Services, (4) Turner School of Theology, and (5) School of Continuing Education. Each of these schools has its own special purpose within the overall purpose and institutional goals of the University. Amridge University 1200 Taylor Road Montgomery, AL 36117 1.888.790.8080 Privacy Policy | Terms and Use | Employment | Amridge Spirit Shop Amridge University © Close Close Accessibility by WAH About Amridge University Capital Prayer Breakfast Statement of a Positive Biblical Faith Employment News Amridge University Press Amridge University President’s Message Academics Academic Catalog Professional Licensure Programs of Study College of General Studies AA in Human Development AA in Legal Studies AA in Liberal Studies AA in Ministry/Bible Minor in Family and Consumer Sciences BA in Biblical Studies BS in Ministry/Bible BS in Human Development BS in Criminal Justice College of Business and Leadership AA in Business Administration AA in Criminal Justice AA in Human Resource Leadership AA Information Systems Manageme